drivers: misc: renesas_drw: fix pp_dlist_indirect_start pointer type

The DRW indirect display-list handling declared pp_dlist_indirect_start
as a double pointer (uint32_t **), but the FSP field
d1_device_flex::pp_dlist_indirect_start is a single pointer
(volatile uint32_t *). Dereferencing the double pointer yields a
uint32_t * that is then assigned to the 32-bit R_DRW->DLISTSTART
register, triggering -Wint-conversion. Under GCC 14 (Zephyr SDK 1.0)
-Wint-conversion is an error by default, so the driver fails to compile
for any Dave2D-accelerated RA board (e.g. ek_ra6m3).

Match FSP's own r_drw_base.c: use a single uint32_t *, dereference it to
the uint32_t display-list address, and compare against 0.

Upstreamable to zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/renesas_drw/renesas_ra_drw.c b/drivers/misc/renesas_drw/renesas_ra_drw.c
index 0960316d7d8..7644062c71e 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/renesas_drw/renesas_ra_drw.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/renesas_drw/renesas_ra_drw.c
@@ -85,10 +85,10 @@ void drw_zephyr_irq_handler(const struct device *dev)
 		d1_device_flex *p_d1_handle = (d1_device_flex *)R_FSP_IsrContextGet(irq);
 
 		if (p_d1_handle != NULL) {
-			uint32_t **pp_dlist_indirect_start =
-				(uint32_t **)p_d1_handle->pp_dlist_indirect_start;
+			uint32_t *pp_dlist_indirect_start =
+				(uint32_t *)p_d1_handle->pp_dlist_indirect_start;
 			if (p_d1_handle->dlist_indirect_enable &&
-			    *pp_dlist_indirect_start != NULL) {
+			    *pp_dlist_indirect_start != 0) {
 				R_DRW->DLISTSTART = *pp_dlist_indirect_start;
 				p_d1_handle->pp_dlist_indirect_start++;
 			} else {
